-- title:
--   Integrally closed fibre model with cusp chart and lifts
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$. Assume given modular polynomial data at level $N$, i.e. a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of $Y$-degree $\psi(N)=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\ \text{squarefree}}N/d$ annihilating the $q$-expansion pair, together with: the relative degree condition that $k(j_q,j_{q,N})=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N` has relative finrank $\psi(N)$ over $k(j_q)$; the coefficient bound $\deg(\Phi.\mathrm{coeff}\,i)\le N(\psi(N)-i)$ for all $i$; and two lifting hypotheses, stating that every $y\in k(j_q,j_{q,N})$ which is a root of a monic polynomial over $k[j_q]$ (respectively over $k[j_q^{-1}]$) is the image under the reduction map `modularRedLocHom` of some $f$ in the localisation of the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the constants $A$ and $j_q,j_{q,N}$ at the prime of elements with nonzero reduction, $f$ being a root of a monic polynomial over $A[j_q]$ (respectively $A[j_q^{-1}]$). Then there exists a `FibreModel N A ℓ k red` satisfying `CuspChart`, whose two chart subrings `BFin`, `BInf` of the base-changed full modular function field are integrally closed, and such that every element $b$ of either chart equals, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, some $f$ in that localised modular ring with $\pi(b)=$ `modularRedLocHom` $f$ in $k((q))$.
--
--   This is the normalisation step for the Kroneckerian (Igusa) model of $X_0(N)$ over a valuation ring: the finite and infinite affine charts of the fibre model are replaced by integrally closed subrings, and the model is kept compatible element-by-element with the coefficientwise reduction of the localised ring of modular functions. It feeds the construction of the reduction of $X_0(N)$ modulo $\ell$ via [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_chartAlg_of_lift`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_chartAlg_of_lift).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_integrallyClosed_of_lift.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_FibreModelCuspChart
